From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: conda-forge nodejs-feedstock <noreply@conda-forge.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Only expose BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH when
 available

conda-forge's brotli 1.2.0 does not define this error code (the -17
BrotliDecoderErrorCode is still reserved in that release), while the
brotli copy vendored by node already does. Since we link against the
system brotli, referencing the constant unconditionally fails to
compile:

  src/node_zlib.cc:2271:32: error: 'BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH'
      was not declared in this scope

build.sh defines NODE_HAVE_BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH when
the system header provides the constant, so it is still exposed to JS
whenever the linked brotli supports it.
---
diff --git a/src/node_zlib.cc b/src/node_zlib.cc
index 3cb736c..f257a1a 100644
--- a/src/node_zlib.cc
+++ b/src/node_zlib.cc
@@ -2268,7 +2268,13 @@ void DefineZlibConstants(Local<Object> target) {
   NODE_DEFINE_CONSTANT(target, BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_PADDING_1);
   NODE_DEFINE_CONSTANT(target, BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_PADDING_2);
   NODE_DEFINE_CONSTANT(target, BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_DISTANCE);
+  // BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH is not part of the brotli 1.2.0
+  // release that conda-forge ships (the -17 error code is still reserved
+  // there), while the copy of brotli vendored by node already defines it.
+  // build.sh only sets this define when the system headers provide it.
+#ifdef NODE_HAVE_BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH
   NODE_DEFINE_CONSTANT(target, BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_FORMAT_BLOCK_SWITCH);
+#endif
   NODE_DEFINE_CONSTANT(target, BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_DICTIONARY_NOT_SET);
   NODE_DEFINE_CONSTANT(target, BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENTS);
   NODE_DEFINE_CONSTANT(target, BROTLI_DECODER_ERROR_ALLOC_CONTEXT_MODES);
